      "writtenOn": "2026-07-13T05:00:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the sole child has default order and the wrapper specifies another order, returning the child directly discards the wrapper\u0027s order.\n\nFor example:\n\n`depset(transitive\u003d[depset([\u0027c\u0027], transitive\u003d[depset([\u0027a\u0027])])], order\u003d\u0027preorder\u0027).to_list()` returns `[\u0027a\u0027, \u0027c\u0027]` instead of `[\u0027c\u0027, \u0027a\u0027]`\n\nI guess the easiest fix would be to only reuse the child when doing so preserves the effective order. (This would also make for a good test case.)",
